From 5909da1f1c4b753fd2dc1cab7f0bce164fdf719f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:08:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/59] CUDA/HIP: LFM2 shortconv in_proj MMVQ with the fused
 conv as per-group ticket tails (GGML_HIP_INPROJ_CONV)

One token: the in_proj MUL_MAT (3 sections of nr rows: x, x2 and gate of the conv) and the fused SSM_CONV of its
output (GGML_HIP_CONV_MUL plan: b*x, conv, c*conv, the q8_1 copy for out_proj, conv-state windows) run as one
kernel (mul_mat_vec_q_conv): a block computes its rows exactly as the plain ncols_dst == 1 kernel (same lanes,
blocks per lane, warp combine, rows per block as GGML_HIP_MMVQ_N1_ROWS), counts them into the ticket of their
32-channel group, and the block that completes a group's 3*32 rows runs ssm_conv_fused_f32_block for those 32
channels with its first warp and resets the ticket. Only when every node between the MUL_MAT and the folded output
MUL runs no kernel; RDNA (the plain kernel is the only n = 1 variant there).

The q8_1 cache buffer now has two slots: a producer writes the slot that is not cached (committed after it), so
the fused kernel can still read the in_proj activations from the cache while its conv tails write the out_proj
activations. Same data, other address.

GGML_HIP_INPROJ_CONV=0: the MMVQ and conv launches.

LFM2.5-24B-A2B Q5_K_M, RX 7900 XTX, KV q8_0: 445 -> 416 kernels/token; mul_mat_vec_q_conv 15.5 us vs in_proj
12.8 + conv 4.7 us plus one launch gap. llama-bench tg128 -r 5, interleaved, 3 rounds: 4.231 -> 4.100 ms/token.

Logit hashes of 64 greedy decode steps (q8_0 KV, depth 0 and 3000) equal to bcdf324d3; greedy md5 LFM plain
(q8_0 KV) 2c7ee8a2..., Qwen plain c4708318..., Qwen MTP 6f14e814... unchanged. test-backend-ops: SHORTCONV 4/4
(new), SSM_CONV 45/45, MUL_MAT 2476/2476, RMS_NORM 53/53, MUL 142/142, NORM_ROUTER_TOPK 5/5, MOE_DOWN_REDUCE 5/5.
